<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Trip Book Maker</title>
<style>
$css
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="lean">
  <header class="masthead">
    <h1>Let's make a trip book</h1>
    <p>Tell us where you're off to. We'll put together a printable activity book —
       puzzles, coloring pages, the works.</p>
  </header>

$message

  <form method="post" action="/generate" enctype="multipart/form-data" class="card">

    <label class="field big">
      <span class="label">Where are you going?</span>
      <input type="text" name="destination" value="$destination" list="known-destinations"
             placeholder="Kfar Hanokdim, Prague, Yellowstone…" required autofocus
             autocomplete="off">
      <span class="hint">Anywhere on earth. We'll dig up the local animals, food and
        landmarks and build the pages around them.</span>
    </label>
    <datalist id="known-destinations">
$known_options
    </datalist>

    <label class="field">
      <span class="label">What's the plan? <em>optional</em></span>
      <textarea name="itinerary" rows="3"
                placeholder="One line per day —&#10;Camels and the big tent&#10;Masada at sunrise&#10;Floating in the Dead Sea">$itinerary</textarea>
      <span class="hint">Skip it if you're winging it. If you do fill it in, the pages
        follow along day by day.</span>
    </label>

    <div class="field">
      <span class="label">Who's coming? <em>optional</em></span>
      <label class="dropzone">
        <input type="file" name="photos" accept="image/*" multiple>
        <span class="dropzone-text">
          <strong>Add a photo or two</strong>
          <small>Then the kids in the drawings can actually look like your kids.</small>
        </span>
      </label>
      <span class="hint">Up to $max_photos pictures. They stay on this machine — they're
        saved next to the book so you can hand them to your image tool as a reference.</span>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <span class="label">Which language?</span>
      <div class="chips">
$language_choices
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="actions">
      <button type="submit">Make my book</button>
      <span class="hint">Give it a couple of seconds.</span>
    </div>
  </form>

  <footer>
    Everything runs on your own machine. The drawings aren't made yet — you get a
    ready-to-paste prompt for each one.
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
